csa26 wraps the open-source static analyzer Cppcheck
(https://cppcheck.sourceforge.io/) and uses its MISRA addon for
checking against MISRA-C:2012 coding guidelines. Cppcheck is
distributed separately under the GNU General Public License v3.0.

MISRA and MISRA C are registered trademarks of The MISRA Consortium
Limited (https://misra.org.uk/). csa26 is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or certified by The MISRA Consortium. References to
MISRA-C:2012 in csa26 documentation, output, and marketing are
factual descriptions of the rule set being checked (nominative fair
use). The verbatim text of MISRA rules is not redistributed by csa26;
rule descriptions in csa26 output are independent paraphrases written
by the csa26 maintainers.

csa26 is a pre-audit tool. It does not constitute a formal
compliance assessment against MISRA-C:2012. Formal compliance
certification remains the responsibility of the user's safety manager.
